      "target": "../sections/sec-002-introduction.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "1. \nThe Fifty-seventh World Health Assembly and the one-hundred-and-thirteenth \nsession of the Executive Board adopted a number of resolutions of regional interest. The \nways and means of implementing the resolutions of interest to the African Region are \ncontained in document AFR/RC54/6 which the Regional Director hereby submits to the fifty-\nfourth session of the Regional Committee for consideration and guidance, in pursuance of \noperative paragraph 5 of resolution AFR/RC30/R12. \n \n2. \nFollowing the Regional Committee’s decisions, guidelines and resolutions, a plan of \nwork will be prepared",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Introduces the report, explaining that it is submitted under an earlier Regional Committee resolution and that a work plan will be prepared to monitor implementation. It begins the section on resolution WHA57.1 on surveillance and control of Buruli ulcer.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/10665-92871/blocks/prose-sec-003",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "REQUESTS the Director-General: to continue to provide technical support to the",
      "pageStart": 3,
      "pageEnd": 4,
      "target": "../sections/sec-003-5-requests-the-director-general-to-continue-to-p.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "REQUESTS the Director-General: to continue to provide technical support to the \nGlobal Buruli Ulcer Initiative, in order particularly to advance understanding of the disease \nburden and to improve early access to diagnosis and treatment by general strengthening of \nhealth infrastructures. \n \n6. \nThe Regional Office will continue to sensitize Member States about the disease and \nprovide guidance to countries on strengthening of health systems with emphasis on planning, \ndecentralization and integration of Buruli ulcer control activities into the existing health \nsystems and to strengthen collab",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes regional action on Buruli ulcer under WHA57.1, including support for the Global Buruli Ulcer Initiative, awareness-raising, integrating control into health systems and links with leprosy, TB and guinea worm programmes. It also mentions surveillance and support for research into better diagnostic, treatment and control tools.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
