        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "WHA57.2: CONTROL OF HUMAN AFRICAN TRYPANOSOMIASIS",
      "pageStart": 4,
      "pageEnd": 5,
      "target": "../sections/sec-004-wha572-control-of-human-african-trypanosomiasis.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The Fifty-seventh World Health Assembly, \n \nOperative paragraph 2.1 \n \n12. \nREQUESTS the Director-General: to continue to refine control strategies so as to \nmake maximum use of national and international resources and to prevent epidemic spread. \n \n13. \nSupport is being provided to countries to elaborate national plans for intensified \ncontrol of human African trypanosomiasis (HAT), with emphasis on case detection and \ntreatment. Support is also provided to control epidemics (Uganda). \n \n14. \nThe Regional Office has developed a database for monitoring of programme \nimplementation. Countries a",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Sets out regional action on resolution WHA57.2 on human African trypanosomiasis, including national plans for intensified case detection and treatment, epidemic control in Uganda and a monitoring database. It also notes drug research through TDR, a WHO–Aventis partnership and the Bill & Melinda Gates Foundation.",
        "state": "draft",
