      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "WHA57.13: GENOMICS AND WORLD HEALTH",
      "pageStart": 8,
      "pageEnd": 9,
      "target": "../sections/sec-010-wha5713-genomics-and-world-health.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The Fifty-seventh World Health Assembly, \n \nOperative paragraph 5.1 \n \n39. \nREQUESTS the Director-General: to provide support to Member States for framing \nnational policies and strategies and strengthening capacity so that they can benefit from the \nadvances in genomics relevant to their health problems and regulatory systems, particularly \nwith regard to safety and the need for public awareness. \n \n40. \nDuring the 2002-2003 biennium, the Regional Office for Africa distributed to all \ncountries in the Region the WHO guidelines for strengthening, establishing and operating \nnational bioethics",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes regional action under resolution WHA57.13 on genomics and world health, such as distributing guidelines on national bioethics committees and plans to build capacity in ethics and genomics. It notes WHO's membership of the EDCTP partnership board as an opportunity to strengthen research capacity.",
        "state": "draft",
